      "text": "To find four consecutive positive integers whose product is 840, we can start by expressing these integers in terms of a variable. Let the four consecutive integers be \\( n, n+1, n+2, n+3 \\). The product of these integers is given by:\n\n\\[ n(n+1)(n+2)(n+3) = 840 \\]\n\nTo estimate the value of \\( n \\), we can find the fourth root of 840. The fourth root of 840 is approximately 5.37, so we can start by trying \\( n = 5 \\):\n\n\\[ 5 \\times 6 \\times 7 \\times 8 = 1680 \\]\n\nSince 1680 is greater than 840, \\( n = 5 \\) is too large. Next, we try \\( n = 4 \\):\n\n\\[ 4 \\times 5 \\times 6 \\times 7 = 840 \\]\n\nThis confirms that the four integers are 4, 5, 6, and 7. Therefore, the largest of the four integers is:\n\n\\[ \\boxed{7} \\]",
